{"user": "Can you explain why playing h1 flipped that whole row of 6 discs? I want to understand what made that work.", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T21:54:02.941571+00:00", "assistant": "Because Othello flips by **bracketing** in a straight line.\n\nWhen Black played **h1**, the top row must have looked like:\n\n**a1 = Black**, then **b1\u2013g1 = White**, and **h1 = empty**\n\nSo after Black placed at **h1**, the row became:\n\n**Black at h1 \u2014 White White White White White White \u2014 Black at a1**\n\nThat means the 6 White discs from **g1 through b1** were trapped between two Black discs, so they all flipped.\n\nKey rule: flips only happen along straight lines where there is an **unbroken chain of opponent discs ending in your disc**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T21:54:02.941571+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T21:54:07.941571+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Board Report": 2}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Board Report": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"